# lsdev(1)

## NAME

lsdev - list connected devices

## SYNOPSIS

    lsdev [-l] [device ...]
    lsdev -w

## DESCRIPTION

Lists the devices connected to the computer, one per line, as `address kind`. An address is a lower-case UUID; a kind looks like `kibicomputers:screen`.

With devices, only the matching ones are listed. A device is named by its whole address, the start of its address, or its kind (`screen` matches `kibicomputers:screen`). Upper-case letters are turned into lower case. A name that matches nothing is reported, and the exit status is 1.

## OPTIONS

- `-l`: list the methods of each device below it, one per line. Methods that run on the game's main thread are marked `(main)`; their results come back on a later tick
- `-w`: after the list, keep watching. A connected device is written as `+ address kind` and a disconnected one as `- address kind`. Stop with Ctrl+C. After the computer is restored from a save, the list is read again and only the differences are written

## SEE ALSO

devcall(1), kibi(7), peripheral(3)
